ia.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-11T17:54:47.139Z"},{"id":"6LedGoDWI","title":"Episode 95: Erik Stenman and The BEAM Book","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/95","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-95-erik-stenman-and-the-beam-book-6ledgodwi","summary":"Erik Stenman, author of The BEAM Book, discusses his programming journey since 1980 and shares insights about the BEAM virtual machine. The conversation covers his extensive experience in tech and his work documenting the BEAM ecosystem through his freely available book.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-23T13:07:47.402Z"},{"id":"lQjrZzM8A","title":"Episode 94: Mike Hostetler and Jido: The Future of Elixir Agents","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/94","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-94-mike-hostetler-and-jido-the-future-of-elixir-agents-lqjrzzm8a","summary":"Mike Hostetler discusses his journey into the Elixir ecosystem and the development of Jido, an autonomous agent framework built for Elixir. The conversation explores how Elixir and the BEAM virtual machine can be leveraged to create intelligent agents, highlighting the unique advantages of functional programming and actor model concurrency for building autonomous systems.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-07-23T05:09:04.227Z"},{"id":"b88fbvEL5","title":"Podcast discussion on Elixir development and community engagement","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/93","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-93-chris-nelson-and-a-riveting-convo-on-elixir-b88fbvel5","summary":"A podcast episode featuring Chris Nelson discussing Elixir development, covering topics like transitioning to Elixir from other languages, the aesthetic appeal of programming languages, and the value of participating in developer meetups and community engagement.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-07-10T15:09:30.576Z"},{"id":"u9S6Bx9Ix","title":"Episode 92: German Velasco and the Advantages of Elixir","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/92","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-92-german-velasco-and-the-advantages-of-elixir-u9s6bx9ix","summary":"BeamRadio hosts discuss the complexities and advantages of Elixir and Phoenix framework with German Velasco, focusing on the benefits for software development and the process of onboarding developers who are transitioning from other programming languages to the Elixir ecosystem.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-27T19:05:33.817Z"},{"id":"LHiqONnHc","title":"Episode 91: BeamRadio Talks Igniter with Zach Daniel","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/91","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-91-beamradio-talks-igniter-with-zach-daniel-lhiqonnhc","summary":"Beam Radio hosts Andrew Ek and Bruce Tate interview Zach Daniel about his experience with Elixir development, focusing on the Ash framework and his new tool called Igniter, which provides code generation and patching capabilities for Elixir projects.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-02T20:49:37.714Z"},{"id":"z3wefMwJR","title":"Episode 89: BeamRadio talks AtomVM - the Erlang virtual machine for IoT devices","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/89","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-89-beamradio-talks-atomvm---the-erlang-virtual-machine-for-iot-devices-z3wefmwjr","summary":"Davide Bettio and Paul Guyot discuss AtomVM, an Erlang virtual machine designed for IoT devices, covering its development process, device compatibility, technical challenges, and future plans.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2025-04-22T15:22:17.353Z"},{"id":"GKXvIEJl8","title":"Episode 88: Unlocking the Power of NX with Paulo Valente","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/88","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-88-unlocking-the-power-of-nx-with-paulo-valente-gkxviejl8","summary":"The post discusses the powerful framework NX for machine learning in Elixir, featuring a deep dive conversation with Lars Wikman, Andrew Ek, and Paulo Valente. It also provides ways to connect with the hosts and Paulo on social platforms.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-07T14:46:24.485Z"},{"id":"bj0qArBq0","title":"Episode 87: Chris Grainger talks Data Science and Engineering and Elixir","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/87","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/episode-87-chris-grainger-talks-data-science-and-engineering-and-elixir-bj0qarbq0","summary":"Lars and Chris discuss the intersection of Elixir with data engineering and data science, focusing on the importance of data pipelines, the role of Elixir in data transformation, and the challenges in data processing.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc4ea15985e43c48aecc3d111deca60?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-21T15:06:17.925Z"},{"id":"dLiB4FwOH","title":"Episode 86: The Future of Gleam: Innovations and Insights with Giacomo Cavalieri","url":"https://www.beamrad.io/86","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/po